  "codebook": {
    "definition": "Credit-claiming occurs when a senator explicitly attributes a positive outcome, action, or achievement to their own efforts, leadership, or advocacy.",
    "clarification": "Credit-claiming is identified when a senator uses first-person language (e.g., 'I secured,' 'I announced,' 'I authored,' 'I fought for') or explicitly ties a positive result to their personal or legislative actions. This includes securing funding, introducing or passing legislation, advocating for a cause, or recognizing others' achievements as a result of their own efforts. The focus is on the senator taking direct or indirect credit for a tangible or intangible benefit.",
